		<title type="html"><![CDATA[setGuiHelper for remote client rendering]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=42908#p42908"><![CDATA[
The GRPC, TCP &amp; UDP client interfaces have a method called setGuiHelper<br>Is there a way this could be leveraged to render a physics scene on a remote client?<br><br>For example; if a web based design tool runs the physic server on a central server; and there are many clients connected from different machines viewing the simulation?<br><br>Any pointers on how to approach this would be most welcome. Looking through the examples; the references to which I could find to setGuiHelper are using DummyGUIHelper; which I understand is a stub.<br><br>Thanks,<br>Brent<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=13619">brent</a> — Sat Jun 13, 2020 1:11 pm</p><hr />
